Committed. Summary of what landed:

**The defect (measured, not hypothesised): `scripts/measure_abstentions.py` anchors every marker to a line `scripts/evolve.sh` prints to the workflow log** — but a `sessions/day-/` directory holds agent transcripts plus files the harness writes into it, never the harness's own stdout. Pointing the tool at a session directory read `fallback=0` by construction*. Confirmed on day-174-20260821T232342Z and day-175-20260822T021038Z: both read fallback=0, both carry `transcripts/plan_retry.log + unverified_task_1.md`, both committed nothing but a wrap-up.

One correction to the task file, worth naming: it said plan_retry.log is at the session dir's top level. It is not — it's in transcripts/. I enumerated all 453 session dirs on audit-log first (as the task itself instructed) and coded against the listing; a test pins that a top-level plan_retry.log does not match.

What shipped:
• classify_structure(relpaths, outcome) — pure, all I/O at the call site (read_outcome is its sibling). Fields: plan_retry (62/453 dirs), unverified (11/453), tasks_attempted/tasks_succeeded.
• Every field three-valued: False = observed-and-absent, UNKNOWN = this stream can't say. Missing outcome.json, absent key, wrong-typed value, and no-listing all report UNKNOWN.
• zero_output is UNKNOWN always, with the reason printed. None of outcome.json's twelve keys and no file records a session's commits, so deriving it from tasks_succeeded would be inventing the number the tool exists to stop inventing. evolve.sh is protected — this makes its `tasks_succeeded: 1` defect visible from outside, nothing more.
• Two streams beside each other, never summed; a ! streams disagree line fires when a retry artifact is present while log-derived fallback=0.

**Verified live:** the two named sessions now show `plan_retry=yes unverified=yes zero_output=unknown` + the disagreement line; the healthy sibling shows `plan_retry=no` (near-miss side exercised for real). A plain log file gets no structure block — old invocations byte-identical.

--test passes; cargo fmt/clippy -D warnings/build/test green (5045 tests, 0 failed). CLAUDE.md bullet updated with the stream mismatch, the artifacts, the never-summed rule, and the zero_output limit.
